title: Red Friday  
new-page: true
subtitle: Mine owners plan to cut wages and increase hours.
view-if: year = 1925 and month = 6
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: dawes_plan_negotiation = 1; dawes_plan_agreed = 1 
tags: event
#face-image: img/portraits/StresemannGustav.jpg

= Red Friday 

The Mine owner's 'Mining Association' has announced that  [? if tories_in_government = 1 : following Mr Churchill's return to the gold standard's impact on coal export profits. That they plan to make cuts to miner's wages and to increase their work hours. ?] [? if labour_in_government = 1 : they plan to make cuts to employee wages and to increase their workhours. ?]

[? if tories_in_government = 1 : The Prime Minister has announced that for the time being, the government shall subsidise the miner's wages and to talk with the mine owners to delay their work hour icnreases. ?]


- @step_forward
- @do_subsidy
- @don_do_subsidy

@step_forward
title: Stay Here's hoping those cuts don't end up happening...
view-if: tories_in_government
on-arrival: unemployed_labour -= 3; workers_labour -= 4; new_middle_labour -= 5; old_middle_labour -= 5; rural_labour -= 4;


@do_subsidy
title: Subsidise their wages for the time being.
view-if: labour_in_government 
on-arrival:  budget -= 1; workers_labour += 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_labour += 6*(1-dissent); welfare += 1; reformist_dissent -= 5; labor_dissent -= 5; center_dissent -= 5; left_dissent -= 5; neorevisionist_dissent -= 5; coalition_dissent += 1 if welfare > 1; welfare_goal_completed += 1; inflation += 0.3; unemployed -= 0.4; economic_growth += 0.2;

This might not work forever, and will likely get more expensive, so we must find a way to resolve this.

@don_do_subsidy
title: We cannot be expected to pick up the bill...
view-if: labour_in_government 
on-arrival: workers_labour -= 6; unemployed_labour -= 6; workers_cpgb += 3; welfare -= 1; reformist_dissent += 10; left_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 10; center_dissent += 5; neorevisionist_dissent += 5; dvp_relation += 5; tories_relation += 3; pro_republic -= 3; coalition_dissent -= 1 if in_grand_coalition and coalition_dissent > 0; kpd_coalition_dissent += 1; cpgb_relation -= 8; inflation -= 0.3; unemployed += 0.4; economic_growth -= 0.2;

This will likely irritate many of our working class supporters. But in economic times like these, it is simply unrealistic to subsidise an entire industry's wages like this.
